      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, if the serpentine belt squeals during acceleration, it's often due to slipping on the pulleys. The belt may need to be replaced, but first, inspect all pulleys for wear or damage and ensure the belt tension is correct according to your vehicle's specifications. Over time, pulley bearings may degrade, causing the belt to skip or slip. Replacing just the belt without addressing these issues might only provide a temporary fix.",
